# RepoWise

This workspace is indexed by [RepoWise](https://github.com/repowise-dev/repowise). Prefer its MCP tools over rediscovering the repo with grep/read loops.

## When to use which tool

| Need | Tool |
|------|------|
| First orientation / architecture | `get_overview` |
| File/module/symbol triage (batch OK) | `get_context` |
| Exact symbol source bounds | `get_symbol` |
| Natural-language question with citations | `get_answer` |
| Wiki / semantic search | `search_codebase` |
| Blast radius / hotspots / PR risk | `get_risk`, `get_change_risk` |
| Why this design | `get_why` |
| Dead code | `get_dead_code` |
| Health + refactoring plans | `get_health` |

## Rules of thumb

1. Call `get_overview` once when the task is unfamiliar.
2. Pass multiple paths/symbols to `get_context` in one call instead of sequential greps.
3. If `_meta.stale_warning` appears, tell the user to run `repowise update` in the repo root.
4. Index is local under `.repowise/` — no cloud required for graph/health/risk tools.

## Keep the index fresh

```bash
repowise update
# or: repowise watch
```
